                        "entry_id": "ffe6235b-7bac-3707-92c6-d00e1b8ee765",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Étoile de neutrons disposant d’un champ magnétique d’une intensité considérable, qui émet des rayonnements électromagnétiques de haute énergie."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6b986014-ae16-4a55-8073-bc833f0a9cea",
                                "sense_id": "0d7b3688-5c0e-3cf3-9ee3-6932d35d5658",
                                "text": "La magnétoile (aimant, magnétisme + étoile) ou «magnetar» dans le texte original (magnet + star), est une découverte récente."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ae0a9d4b-1d8f-497a-91fc-7dd62388f054",
                        "source_entry_id": "ffe6235b-7bac-3707-92c6-d00e1b8ee765",
                        "source_sense_id": "0d7b3688-5c0e-3cf3-9ee3-6932d35d5658",
                        "target_lang_word": "magnetar",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "magnetar",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a99c57af-59cd-3a2f-a6f6-cac82ce3ce39",
                                        "entry_id": "a71fec6a-4d24-3cad-bbfb-8c87388bc2bf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A neutron star or pulsar with an extremely powerful magnetic field, especially those on which starquakes occur, thought to be the source of some gamma-ray bursts."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "46e322cb-a0e3-4d5c-ac53-728e2442445c",
                                                "sense_id": "a99c57af-59cd-3a2f-a6f6-cac82ce3ce39",
                                                "text": "This signal could be detected with Advanced LIGO-class detectors up to the distance of the Virgo cluster, where ≥ 1 yr⁻¹ magnetars are expected to form."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c65f7ca1-46af-4a00-96fb-7003eaa5f262",
                                                "sense_id": "a99c57af-59cd-3a2f-a6f6-cac82ce3ce39",
                                                "text": "2008, W. Becker, F, Haberl, J Trümper, 14: Pulsars and Isolated Neutron Stars, Joachim E. Trümper, Günther Hasinger (editors), The Universe in X-Rays, page 193,\nThe radio-silent neutron stars include anomalous X-ray pulsars (AXPs), soft gamma-ray repeaters (SGRs), and “quiescent” neutron star candidates in SNRs. There is growing evidence that AXPs and SGRs are indeed magnetars (see [109] for a review)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "375fc449-2435-43a1-aca7-80ffd2654e87",
                                                "sense_id": "a99c57af-59cd-3a2f-a6f6-cac82ce3ce39",
                                                "text": "One of most mysterious feature[s] of magnetars is their X-ray luminosities, which always exceed the rotational energy loss. Thus, the energy source of the radiation of magnetars is a mysterious question."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
